        "title": "refactor(copilot): use SDK session and tool-result contracts",
        "body": "Closes #106192\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nCopilot plugin maintenance duplicated contracts already owned by the pinned Copilot SDK: session-compaction configuration and MCP tool-result conversion. The copies added 225 net lines of drift-prone code and tests.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nForward `SessionConfig[\"infiniteSessions\"]` directly and use the SDK's public `convertMcpCallToolResult` helper for successful tool output. OpenClaw keeps its own execution-failure and lifecycle-error handling; SDK-owned defaults, validation, and result conversion stay with the SDK.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intended user-visible behavior change. The Copilot plugin has less local compatibility code and follows the exact pinned SDK contracts.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Net change: 13 insertions, 238 deletions (225 fewer lines).\n- Direct dependency proof: `@github/copilot-sdk` 1.0.5 publicly exports `convertMcpCallToolResult`; `SessionConfig` owns `infiniteSessions`. The pinned Copilot CLI 1.0.68 applies identical defaults for omitted and empty infinite-session config while preserving explicit values.\n- Focused Blacksmith Testbox run [29235869371](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29235869371): 193 tests passed across `attempt.test.ts` and `tool-bridge.test.ts`.\n- Same Testbox lease: `pnpm check:changed` passed.\n- Same Testbox lease: `pnpm build` passed.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Fresh pre-commit and post-rebase autoreviews: no actionable findings.\n\nAI assistance: Codex audited the dependency contracts, implemented the refactor, and ran validation. Maintainer reviewed the resulting diff and evidence.\n",
